---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="Where to Swim in MBR City"
  description="Looking for where to actually swim in MBR City? The honest breakdown: building pools, District One's Crystal Lagoon (and who actually has access), and the drive to the sea."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Water</p>
    <h1>Where to actually swim</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      MBR City has two real water features — District One's Crystal Lagoon
      and the Riviera canal — plus the standard building-pool amenity most
      communities share. Here's which of those you can actually swim in.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>District One's Crystal Lagoon</h2>
    <p>
      The district's most distinctive water feature: a large artificial
      lagoon with clear turquoise water, ringed by a running and cycling
      track. It reads as the closest thing to a beach in MBR City, but
      access is tied to the surrounding District One villas rather than
      open district-wide — if you're not a District One resident, confirm
      access terms directly rather than assuming it's a public amenity.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>The Riviera canal — not a swim spot</h2>
    <p>
      The Dubai Water Canal running along Azizi Riviera is active boat and
      water-taxi traffic, not a designated swimming area, despite how
      waterfront renders make it look. See
      <a href="https://riviera.dst.llc/water/">Riviera's own water page</a>
      for the full version of that distinction.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Building pools</h2>
    <p>
      For most residents across the district, a shared building pool — see
      the <a href="/pools/">pools page</a> — is the realistic day-to-day
      answer, not the lagoon or the canal.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>The actual sea</h2>
    <p>
      Kite Beach, La Mer, and JBR are the nearest public beaches, roughly a
      20–30 minute drive regardless of which MBR City community you're
      starting from. There's no direct transit link — a car or taxi is the
      realistic way to get there.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: var(--space-5); }
  .lede { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--ink-muted); max-width: 65ch; }
</style>
